CYWS (The Change You Want to See)

CYWS is by Ragav Sachdeva and Andrew Zisserman (The Change You Want to See,
WACV 2023, https://github.com/ragavsachdeva/The-Change-You-Want-to-See).
The authors have confirmed to the maintainer (2026) that CYWS, its code and
pretrained weights, is released under the Apache License 2.0. This supersedes
the CC BY-NC default mentioned in upstream issue #11 (2024). The upstream
repository does not include a LICENSE file yet.

model/cyws_mla.py is an independent reimplementation of the CYWS architecture.
Its module names match the upstream checkpoint so that the pretrained weights
load unchanged. Files derived from the weights (the checkpoint with BatchNorm
folded, the ONNX export and the compiled MPKs) are also Apache-2.0.

